RF.put("questb:b0",{"8560":{"id":8560,"t":"Conqueror's Legguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ouro's Intact Hide, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nOuro's Intact Hide Ouro\n2 Idol of Death Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"You seek to prove your worth to my kind, mortal? Very well, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.\nThe ancient sandworm, Ouro, is a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God himself as a mockery of life.\nHis skin is unnatural... thick, nearly impregnable, yet it's flexible and allows him to move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature.\nBring me a sample of his skin along with other minor components and I shall craft you leggings of great power.","rew":"You will receive:\nConqueror's Legguards\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"Yes... the worm's hide will make for an excellent protective layer. Combined with the strongest parts from the Qiraji we've destroyed on our way here, this should make for a formidable piece of armor. May it aid you in facing the unspeakable horrors that await inside!\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warrior Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8560\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Conqueror's Legguards this quest\nBring Ouro's Intact Hide, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8640":{"id":8640,"t":"Deathdealer's Leggings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ouro's Intact Hide, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nOuro's Intact Hide Ouro\n2 Idol of Night Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"You seek to prove your worth to my kind, mortal? Very well, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.\nThe ancient sandworm, Ouro, is a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God himself as a mockery of life.\nHis skin is unnatural... thick, nearly impregnable, yet it's flexible and allows him to move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature.\nBring me a sample of his skin along with other minor components and I shall craft you leggings of great power.","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathdealer's Leggings\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Rogue Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8640\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Deathdealer's Leggings this quest\nBring Ouro's Intact Hide, 2 Idols of Night, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"93680":{"id":93680,"t":"Key to the city","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Acquire the Dalaran Sewer Key for Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill.\nGrimy Key","desc":"The Alliance had an army of mages known as the Kirin Tor. While they were powerful, the demonic Burning Legion proved to be even more so. In one fell swoop, the arch demon Archimonde flattened their city like it was a child's plaything. Those who remained were reduced to merely dispossessed vagabonds.\nThat is, until they rebuilt Dalaran. And on the Dark Lady's very doorstep, no less!\nWhile in their camps, search for something that can get us into the city unnoticed. I must know more.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.6,"y":20.8,"n":"Magus Wordeen Voidglare","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"8160":{"id":8160,"t":"Cut Arathor Supply Lines","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,900 experience instead of 5,500, 0.71 times as much.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Deathstalker Mortis at Hammerfall.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"The League of Arathor is sparing no expense in their move to retake Arathi. They, and all the races of the Alliance, now stream to this distant region, intent on expanding their hold from Refuge Pointe. We must stop them, and the best means to stop them is to take their supplies.\nYou can help us, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, known for its rich mines, fertile land and skilled craftsman. Capture and control every base you can, win the battle, and return to me with the resources you gain.","rew":"Money: 1 95 1 gold, 95 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+200 reputation with The Defilers\nLevel 45 , requires level 40 Difficulty 40 41 43 48 57 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable No Quest ID 8160","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8080":{"id":8080,"t":"Arathi Basin Resources!","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,650 experience instead of 8,150, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.\nArathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you. They'll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!\nThat is why Arathi Basin is important. There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources. Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.\nThat is what I want from you, ‹name›. Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.","rew":"Money: 2 50 2 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Do you have the resource crate, ‹name›? The League of Arathor can't fight a decent battle without them...","done":"You got the resources! Great job! I'll send the resources to our quartermasters, who can quickly disperse them to our troops.\nThank you, ‹name›. Indeed, performing successful missions like the one you achieved are how wars are truly won.\nLevel 55 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 51 53 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable No Quest ID 8080","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"640":{"id":640,"t":"The Broken Sigil","lv":40,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the 5 Sigil Fragments from the defenders in Stromgarde, and bring them to Tor'gan in Hammerfall.\n5 Sigil Fragment Stromgarde Vindicator 80 % , Stromgarde Defender 80 % , Stromgarde Troll Hunter 80 %","desc":"Thoras Trollbane's tomb is protected by three sigils--the first of which you retrieved from the Syndicate. The other two will be harder to get, as they're held by the firmly entrenched Stromgarde militia.\nThe sigil of Thoradin was divided into five pieces by Thoras' son, Galen, and dispersed among the Stromgarde defenders. Retrieve the pieces and bring them to Tor'gan, the troll shaman, he will be able to bind them into the complete sigil.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Throm'ka, ‹class›. Zengu informed me that you required my assistance?","done":"Ah, you need me to reconstruct this sigil? It shouldn't be too difficult... all the pieces seem to be here and the magical structure will be easy to reform.\nYou might want to close your eyes.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.8,"y":34,"n":"Zengu","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1040":{"id":1040,"t":"Passage to Booty Bay","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take a boat to Booty Bay and speak with Caravaneer Ruzzgot.","desc":"Ah yes, finally found it. Should have told me she passed through here that long ago. Let's see.\nVelinde. Booked passage to Booty Bay on the Black Osprey. I don't have anything here saying otherwise, so I'd assume it arrived in port safely.\nNot much more help I can be to you, but she asked about overland travel over on that side of the world, and I mentioned Ruzzgot, a caravan driver based out of Booty Bay. Might be that this Velinde traveled with him.\nMove along, now. I haven't all day for you.","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Booty Bay","done":"Yes? Now, it doesn't look to me like you're the sort with goods that need shipping, so either you're looking for a job with my caravan--and there's no jobs to be had now--or you're probably talking to the wrong goblin.\nSo which one is it?\nThe Barrens Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.4,"y":38.5,"n":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.4,"y":74.1,"n":"Caravaneer Ruzzgot","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"720":{"id":720,"t":"A Sign of Hope","lv":35,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Prospector Ryedol and let him know Hammertoe Grez is alive.","desc":"<There is text roughly scribbled in chalk on the map.>\n\"Ryedol,\nThey're taking me to Uldaman. Send help.\n-Hammertoe\"","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Hammertoe's alive?! This is amazin', ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":53,"y":33.9,"n":"Crumpled Map","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":53.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Prospector Ryedol","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"1200":{"id":1200,"t":"Blackfathom Villainy","lv":27,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 7,850 experience instead of 1,700, 4.62 times as much. New rewards: Dark Ritual Leggings, Cultist's Armguards. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeo","obj":"Bring the head of Twilight Lord Kelris to Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus.\nHead of Kelris Twilight Lord Kelris","desc":"Strength has left me. Your help is needed!\nLong ago this site was a great temple of Elune. But misfortune led to ruin when the corruption of an Old God seeped up from beneath the earth and tainted the sacred Moon Well.\nAku'Mai, servant of the Old God, rose from the waters.\nThe Twilight's Hammer cultists have allied with the naga to occupy these grounds. The cultists, led by Kelris, sacrifice innocents to Aku'Mai for power.\nSlay Kelris and bring his head to Selgorm in Darnassus, ‹name›, please.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGravestone Scepter Arctic Buckler Dark Ritual Leggings Cultist's Armguards\nNew in Forever: Dark Ritual Leggings, Cultist's Armguards.\nMoney: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,850\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+200 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Time is a precious commodity, ‹class›.\nMy role here in Darnassus is to ensure that the Argent Dawn thrives and that the evil forces encroaching upon Kalimdor are thwarted.\nState your business quickly or be on your way.","done":"Kelris has eluded us for quite some time.\nIt seems as though whenever evil made its presence known in these parts, Kelris had played a role. For some time we considered him dead or missing.\nBut this makes perfect sense. By ending his reign you have spared the lives of many innocent people.\nBy the light! To sacrifice someone to a servant of an Old God for one's personal gain is beyond reproachful!\nYou have done a great deed, ‹name›. I salute you on behalf of the Argent Dawn.\nDarnassus Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":56.2,"y":24.4,"n":"Dawnwatcher Selgorm","e":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"8960":{"id":8960,"t":"Bodley's Unfortunate Fate","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Mountain and use the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer to find Bodley near Blackrock Spire.","desc":"So we need to recover the rest of the medallion? Finding Bodley's going to be a bit of a headache. He went back to Blackrock Mountain to attempt to re-enter Blackrock Spire and never came back.\nI'd suggest taking the goblin's ghost revealing device with you, as I fear the worst might have happened.","rew":"Experience: 1,650","done":"I am so glad that you can see me. Finally someone to talk to!\nWill you help us, ‹name›? Help to undo the wrong that we perpetrated and put things to right? If it's true that you already have the Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet, then I think I can point you in the right direction to acquire the other two parts, reunite them and put an end to all of this.\nOh, by the way, hello, my name is Bodley. Nice to meet you!\nDun Morogh Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"97920":{"id":97920,"t":"Camping 101 fishing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Lee Brown near Goldshire to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your fishing skill to 20","desc":"You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.","back":"I can teach you once you've gained some skill as a fisherman.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":47.4,"y":62.2,"n":"Lee Brown","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94320":{"id":94320,"t":"Craftsmans writ gift of arthas","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Gift of Arthas\nGift of Arthas","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Gift of Arthas, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Gift of Arthas Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94320","cats":["crafting"]},"94240":{"id":94240,"t":"Craftsmans writ herbalists gloves","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Herbalist's Gloves\nHerbalist's Gloves","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Herbalist's Gloves, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Herbalist's Gloves Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94240","cats":["crafting"]},"960":{"id":960,"t":"Onu is meditating","lv":1,"min":12,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Onu is meditating.","rew":"You will receive:\nPhial of Scrying","done":"I am meditating on your task, ‹name›. Meditating on reasons why the Twilight's Hammer and naga are here.\nWhen you are ready, use the phial of scrying to create a scrying bowl. Then, contact me through the bowl.\nIf you have lost your phial of scrying, then here is another.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.3,"n":"Onu","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"87760":{"id":87760,"t":"Holy diver","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find a Stormscale Beastmistress, slay her, and bring back her Rod of Deep Dominion.\nRod of Deep Dominion","desc":"I have received word back from Darnassus, ‹name›!\nFrom the animal samples, we learned that the naga dominated these sea creatures to use as unwilling mounts and beasts of burden. The ones that were too obstinate, or too old or badly injured, they drove out for sport. Monstrous!\nIt is our sacred duty to put a stop to this!\nThe naga have forces in the Ruins of Mathystra, and they must be seizing threshers from off the shore. Find their beastmistress, slay her, and bring back her tools of domination!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Draught of Water Breathing 5 Swim Speed Potion\nMoney: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"We will finally have resolution to this mystery, and the animals will have peace at last!","done":"This has been a long journey, Orangequake, but it was worth it.\nAt long last, you have wrested away the rod that the naga use to compel the sea creatures into their service. I will make sure it is destroyed, and the threshers and sea turtles can finally live in peace.\nThank you again. Your persistence has finally been rewarded, and I, personally, am grateful to you.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1440":{"id":1440,"t":"Return to Vahlarriel","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Dalinda Malem from Thunder Axe Fortress and then return to Vahlarriel Demonslayer in Desolace.","desc":"So, the time is now then? I appreciate your efforts, and if the situation does not lend itself, then allow me to thank you now for everything you've done for me and my family. If you're ready, then there is nothing else for me here--we can leave when you feel the time is right.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGrappler's Belt Gloves of Insight Garrison Cloak Moonlit Amice\nExperience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Dalinda made it safely back here to Nijel's Point, and in much better condition than I could have asked for. The fact that she arrived here under her own power was a good sign. I hope you're well?\nIt pains me to know that both Tyranis and Dalinda didn't return, but the embarrassment of Tyranis' decisions is hers to endure. It is something she will have to deal with when she returns to Darnassus.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":54.9,"y":26.1,"n":"Dalinda Malem","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":66.4,"y":11.8,"n":"Vahlarriel Demonslayer","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"3120":{"id":3120,"t":"Verdant Sigil","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Verdant Sigil and speak to Mardant Strongoak, in the tree Aldrassil in Shadowglen.\nVerdant Sigil\nProvided: Verdant Sigil","desc":"This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our druid trainer, Mardant. It seems Mardant would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to him afterwards.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Ah, young ‹class›. I see you're eager to continue your studies. Good.\nI wonder, have you spent much time in the Emerald Dream already? Perhaps you're not prepared for that yet... In time, I'm sure.\nBut until then, we should discuss other matters.","done":"I will be your mentor and guide for now. It is my duty to teach you how to interpret not only what the spirits communicate to us, but also the complexities and secrets of the Emerald Dream.\nAs you learn and grow in power, you will learn more of our sleeping trance. But until then, return to me as often as you like and I will teach you what I can in the ways of our kind.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.7,"y":44.3,"n":"Conservator Ilthalaine","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.6,"y":40.3,"n":"Mardant Strongoak","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"2160":{"id":2160,"t":"Supplies to Tannok","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Crate of Inn Supplies to Tannok Frosthammer in Kharanos.\nCrate of Inn Supplies\nProvided: Crate of Inn Supplies","desc":"Hey! You look like a hearty adventurer. If you're planning on braving the pass, do you suppose you could bring a package to the inn in Kharanos?\nYou were planning on stopping at the inn, right? If you make it through the pass, you'll definitely want to take a breather there.\nAnyways, bring this to Tannok Frosthammer, the innkeeper's assistant. I can't get through the pass myself, and it'll be days until a Mountaineer escort comes through!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Tough Jerky 5 Refreshing Spring Water\nExperience: 110\n+25 reputation with Ironforge\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Hi there! Come in, take a seat by the fire and warm yourself with a flagon of ale.","done":"Ah, at last, the supplies from Hands! I was beginning to worry, we've had scarce word from Anvilmar ever since the troggs overran the pass.\nThanks for bring this to me, ‹name›. And please, make yourself comfortable. You must be tired after your journey.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":33.8,"y":72.2,"n":"Hands Springsprocket","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.2,"y":52.2,"n":"Tannok Frosthammer","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"400":{"id":400,"t":"Tools for Steelgrill","lv":5,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 110 experience instead of 100, 1.1 times as much.","obj":"Deliver Steelgrill's Tools to Beldin Steelgrill.\nSteelgrill's Tools\nProvided: Steelgrill's Tools","desc":"Beldin Steelgrill owns the local mechanic shop, and he's the best siege engine tech there is! But he's not forgiving to his tools. I swear he almost breaks more arclight spanners than we can supply him with!\nWe just filled his last order for tools. If you deliver it to him I'm sure he'll make it worth the effort.\nHis shop, Steelgrill's Depot, is just northeast of Kharanos. And it's a local haunt for veteran siege engine pilots, so keep your ears open for opportunities while you're there.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 0 silver, 25 copper Experience: 110\n+25 reputation with Ironforge\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Hm? You look a little young to be a siege engine pilot. But no matter...do you need something fixed?\nWell take a number and get comfortable. I'm working on a couple engines right now and won't have time for another job for at least a few days.\nOr, were you here for something else...?","done":"You have my tools? Well done, lad, well done! I just broke my last fang-ratchet an hour ago and I need one of those to finish repairs on Pilot Stonegear's siege engine. You did a good thing by lugging those tools here, ‹name›.\nHere, take these coins for your help.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46,"y":51.7,"n":"Tharek Blackstone","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":50.4,"y":49.1,"n":"Beldin Steelgrill","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"320":{"id":320,"t":"Return to Bellowfiz","lv":8,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give the cask of Evershine to Pilot Bellowfiz at Steelgrill's Depot.\nCask of Evershine\nProvided: Cask of Evershine","desc":"Here's your cask of Evershine, ‹name›. And again, thank you for the hunting earlier.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSharp Axe Gnarled Short Staff Camping Knife\nExperience: 875\n+150 reputation with Ironforge\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Did you get that Evershine?","done":"Yes, this will do just fine. I think I'll open a bottle right now and have a taste...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":30.2,"y":45.7,"n":"Rejold Barleybrew","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":49.4,"y":48.4,"n":"Pilot Bellowfiz","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"240":{"id":240,"t":"Return to Jitters","lv":20,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Jitters with the Dusky Crab Cakes.\nDusky Crab Cakes\nProvided: Dusky Crab Cakes","desc":"And here we are - \"Crab\" Cakes ala Grual!","rew":"Money: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, you're here! Do you have my food?!?","done":"Aha! Thank you, ‹name›. Those really hit the spot!\nAnd here, please let me pay you for these!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Chef Grual","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":18.4,"y":56.4,"n":"Jitters","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"80":{"id":80,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Show Clerk Daltry the Bloodstained Journal Page.\nA Bloodstained Journal Page\nProvided: A Bloodstained Journal Page","desc":"I have had my eye on that creep, Stalvan, for quite sometime. But if this page was written by the same hand it proves his guilt beyond a shadow of a doubt.\nIn all his days keeping the Town Registry, Clerk Daltry has become an expert at identifying handwriting. Show him this page and see if the writing matches that of the registry signature.","rew":"Experience: 230\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Back again, ‹name›? What do you have this time?","done":"Why yes! The writing on this page does in fact match that of the registry signatures.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"160":{"id":160,"t":"Note to the Mayor","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Abercrombie's Letter to Ello Ebonlocke, Mayor of Darkshire.\nLetter to Ello\nProvided: Letter to Ello","desc":"Take this note to Ello Ebonlocke, the Mayor of Darkshire.\nHe and I are old friends...and when he reads it and discovers what you did for me...I'm sure he'll be just as happy as I am! Hahahaha!","rew":"Experience: 600","back":"Abercrombie...? I don't know a person of that name. You say you have a letter for me from this Abercrombie fellow?\nWell let's have it then...","done":"<Ello looks at the letter...>\nWhat language is this? It looks ancient...I can't read it.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":28.1,"y":31.5,"n":"Abercrombie","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":71.9,"y":46.4,"n":"Lord Ello Ebonlocke","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9200":{"id":9200,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Major Mana Potion","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 10 Major Mana Potions and the Craftsman's Writ - Major Mana Potion - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Major Mana Potion\n10 Major Mana Potion Quartermaster Zigris , Imperial Qiraji Destroyer 30 % , Colossal Anubisath Warbringer 30 % , Lieutenant General Nokhor 25 % and 4 more\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Major Mana Potion","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order AL-473:\n10 Major Mana Potions.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"The utility of these should go without saying.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"560":{"id":560,"t":"Farren's Proof","lv":32,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the sack of murloc heads to Marshall Redpath in Southshore.\nSack of Murloc Heads\nProvided: Sack of Murloc Heads","desc":"You know, ‹name›, I'd really rather not take these heads... Since you've already got a handle on them, would you mind delivering them to Redpath for me?","rew":"Experience: 260\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Greetings, citizen. Have you come to lend your arm to upholding the safety of Southshore?","done":"Farren's errand boy, are you?\nIf you assisted Farren in procuring these heads, then thank you. Southshore needs hard workers and effort to maintain its protection.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Lieutenant Farren Orinelle","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":49.5,"y":58.7,"n":"Marshal Redpath","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"8880":{"id":8880,"t":"Cluster Rockets","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will receive:\nCluster Rocket Recipes Lunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"Cluster rockets are a collection of individual rockets, and their beauty is awesome! Bring me coins of ancestry and I will share the knowledge of their creation to you...","done":"Here you are, ‹name›. Take these recipes and learn their secrets. I bid you fortune, and I look forward to seeing your magnificent creations.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.8,"y":35.3,"n":"Fariel Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8720":{"id":8720,"t":"Skygleam the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":72.6,"y":85.2,"n":"Elder Skygleam","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1920":{"id":1920,"t":"Investigate the Blue Recluse","lv":16,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain a Cantation of Manifestation and a Chest of Containment coffers from behind Jennea Cannon. Bring 3 Filled Containment Coffers to Jennea at the Wizard's Sanctum.\n3 Filled Containment Coffer Filled Containment Coffer\nChest of Containment Coffers Chest of Containment Coffers\nCantation of Manifestation Cantation of Manifestation","desc":"A disturbance has been reported at the Blue Recluse tavern in the Mage Quarter. Strange, invisible creatures now wander the tavern, and I fear a mana rift has formed there.\nI want you to investigate the tavern and capture those creatures. Use the cantation of manifestation in the tavern to make the creatures visible, subdue them then use a containment coffer to capture them. When you have enough, return to me with your filled coffers, your empty coffers and the cantation.","rew":"Experience: 1,150","back":"Have you captured the creatures, ‹name›? They must be studied in order to determine the reason behind their arrival.","done":"Very well done! I will study these creatures and, with diligence and luck, determine how they slipped into our world.\nYour value to the society of mages grows, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":85.8,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"76160":{"id":76160,"t":"Stalk with the earthmother","lv":11,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 8 Windfury Cones north of Thunder Bluff, use them with the Mortar and Pestle, then return to Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff with the result.\nPine Salve\n8 Windfury Cone","desc":"Maybe your skills lie with poisons, not disguises. The Harpies to the north nest in a tree which produces a resin of potent toxicity. Gather the fallen cones around the nests, then crush them into a salve. When applied to a blade this salve will sear your opponent's wounds into their flesh and turn their blood to salt.","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 206177\nExperience: 650","back":"Be careful with the salve once you are finished, ‹class›. Even skin contact could be quite painful.","done":"‹class›, this is not the venomous salve I asked for. What you have brought me is pine nut butter. Are you sure you followed my instructions?\nThis will be of far more use spread on some spice bread than on a dagger. Although you would be quite formidable against a foe with a nut allergy.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":39.6,"y":65.6,"n":"Boarton Shadetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"76240":{"id":76240,"t":"Stalk with the earthmother","lv":11,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Buy or catch a Raw Brilliant Smallfish, then use the Knife Set to fillet it in front of Boarton Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff.\nFish Chunks","desc":"I have one last idea that may lead us to success. I still feel there is hidden talent in you, but let us try and coax it out with a less direct approach.\nGo and procure a Raw Brilliant Smallfish, then bring it back here. Use these daggers to clean and fillet it. Do not think too hard - do what comes naturally.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHoof-Holstered Blade Valley Cosh\nExperience: 875","back":"Do you have something for me?","done":"That was quite a display, ‹class›. Not the rogueish precision I hoped for, but you possess an impressive ambidexterity.\nI see now that you will not be the one to train my people in the subtle arts, but there is one thing I can teach you. Good luck on your travels, ‹class›. The Horde will need heroes like you.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":39.6,"y":65.6,"n":"Boarton Shadetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9040":{"id":9040,"t":"Dreadnaught Gauntlets","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreadnaught Gauntlets if you bring him the following items: 1 Desecrated Gauntlets, 8 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 5 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Gauntlets\n8 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n5 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"During your battles with the Scourge in Naxxramas, should you come across desecrated battlements and wartorn plate scraps, return them to me and I shall craft for you a piece of armor worn by heroes.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreadnaught Gauntlets\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Dreadnaught Gauntlets.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9120":{"id":9120,"t":"The Fall of Kel'Thuzad","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 14,300, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Take the Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad to Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nThe Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad Kel'Thuzad in Naxxramas\nProvided: The Phylactery of Kel'Thuzad","desc":"The phylactery is all that remains of the master of Naxxramas. Your better judgment dictates that you destroy the phylactery, preventing the lich from ever reforming. Thankfully, you seldom listen to that internal voice of reason.\nSomeone at Light's Hope will pay you hugely for this artifact. Who cares if Kel'Thuzad regenerates to full power?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMark of the Champion Mark of the Champion\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Father Inigo Montoy","e":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"5680":{"id":5680,"t":"Shadowguard","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Ur'kyo in Ogrimmar.","desc":"Like many of our own priests, your own tribe puts you through rites of passage. These rites often teach priests special abilities that are vital to their survival. I sense that time is upon you even as we speak. You must return to the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar and speak to Ur'kyo. What he teaches you might be very important for the future.","rew":"You will learn: Shadowguard","done":"Your rites will come soon enough. For now, I teach you a spell that will be of great use to you when you do battle with your enemies.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.7,"y":86.9,"n":"Zayus","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":87.8,"n":"Ur'kyo","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"2480":{"id":2480,"t":"Hinott's Assistance","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Serge Hinott to complete the cure.","desc":"I have never seen such wondrous results from a poison! Zanzil you say? Never heard of him, however, I must commend him on the creation of this concoction.\nSo, I am to cure you of this and then teach you how to make use of the poison?\nGive me a few moments to examine the toxin, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nHinott's Oil\nYou will learn: Poisons\nExperience: 160","done":"The cure is ready! Drink this anti-toxin and the creeping madness will stop, however, I will not be able to do anything about the smell.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.6,"y":19.2,"n":"Serge Hinott","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"96800":{"id":96800,"t":"Past due","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Retrieve the book The Lost Magic of the Runemasters from the Scarlet Monastery.\nThe Lost Magic of the Runemasters","desc":"You there, ‹class›. I have a matter I could use assistance with.\nI just so happen to be writing a thesis on the ancient Wildhammer runemasters of Grim Batol, and there's a particular tome I need to complete my research. According to our ledgers, a mage by the name of Doan checked the book out of the old Dalaran library before the Third War and never returned it!\nArcanist Doan is now holed up in the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades. Retrieve this book for me and you'll be well rewarded.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSalve and Salvation Knucklebound Thimble\nMoney: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,750\n+100 reputation with Kirin Tor","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":9.8,"y":63,"n":"Magus Olvek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scarlet-monastery"]},"1520":{"id":1520,"t":"Call of Earth","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 180 experience instead of 200, 0.9 times as much.","obj":"Find Kodo Rock and drink the Earth Sapta.\nProvided: Earth Sapta","desc":"A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the open minded to see the elements as no one has seen them before. Your spirit will forever be tied to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few of our kind know the secrets of its creation.\nThe sapta is always imbibed in a holy place, and never anywhere else.\nSeek out the shaman shrine to the east of here and drink of the sapta.","rew":"Experience: 180","done":"Ah... ‹name›... pleased is the earth to have you here.\nBound together in body and spirit, you will go forward knowing that the mountains are your strength; the plains, your patience; and the world itself your essence.\nStanding before the earth humbly is all that is required of you for you to pass this rite. But the others are not as passive. They may be chaotic and often violent, but such is the nature of the elements. Dual natures opposing one another, you must come to learn these things intricately.\nMulgore Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.3,"y":76.8,"n":"Seer Ravenfeather","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":52,"y":80.4,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","e":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":44,"y":76.2,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8800":{"id":8800,"t":"Cenarion Battlegear","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.","desc":"As you complete the tasks you're assigned in the war you'll want to talk to Vargus, the blacksmith. Show him any badges you've earned along the way. He'll provide you with gear to match your level of commitment to our cause.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+10 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Kaldon sent you? Very well, let's see what we can do for you.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50,"y":36.4,"n":"Windcaller Kaldon","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Vargus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8320":{"id":8320,"t":"Twilight Geolords","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Twilight Geolords, then return to Huum Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\nTwilight Geolord slain : 0/ 10","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer, an insane cult bent on destruction, set up camps in Silithus and perform rituals day and night. We do not yet know their plans, but we do think they are somehow linked to the pulsing red crystals spread across the desert.\nAlthough their mystery may one day be solved, we must first deal with their immediate threat. Go to their camps to the west and seek out Twilight geolords. They are the heads of these serpents; that is where we must strike!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Enter the desert and find the Twilight geolords, ‹name›. Return to me after they are slain.","done":"That was a task well performed, ‹name›. Your slaying of the Twilight geolords must have dealt a grievous blow to the cult. Let us hope their plans are slowed...","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.9,"n":"Huum Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"91920":{"id":91920,"t":"Wild eyes","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 3 murloc eyes and bring them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.\n3 Murloc Eye","desc":"I wouldn't dare to question the effectiveness of Apothecary Renferrel's formulae, however I would be lying if I said that the potion made any noticeable difference.\nAlong the shore of Lake Lordamere are a swarm of murlocs, and of note, murlocs have eyes. I suspect the apothecary's willingness to try new things is suppressed by his recent obsession with hearts. Bring him a few.\nIf my choice is to inevitably die a second death or have Renferrel kill me for questioning his methods, I choose the latter.","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Minor Discolored Healing Potion Minor Discolored Healing Potion\nMoney: 2 0 gold, 2 silver, 0 copper Experience: 440\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Oh. You're back?","done":"The potion didn't work? Of course it didn't work. You brought me insufficient hearts. The recipe clearly calls for six. You brought three.\nHowever, I confess I hadn't considered applications for murloc parts until now...\n<Renferrel takes the eyes.>\nI can afford to sacrifice a few of my own hearts to get your Deathstalker's strength back.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":53.4,"y":12.6,"n":"Quinn Yorick","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.8,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"480":{"id":480,"t":"The Weaver","lv":22,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill the Dalaran archmage, then retrieve his staff for Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.\nAtaeric's Staff Archmage Ataeric","desc":"An archmage of great power is overseeing the reactivation of the ley energy node. With the progress they have made, our only hope of stopping them is by killing him. It will be difficult, he is no doubt protected by many other mages and warders.\nYou must go, and you must dispatch him quickly. When he is dead, retrieve his staff for me. Go now.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCeranium Rod Camouflaged Tunic\nExperience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Quickly, time runs short, ‹name›!","done":"The magic of the wizards dissipates, and the ley energies fade into dormancy. Your efforts have been fruitful, ‹name›, and we have dealt a major blow to our enemies, and to the overbearing wizards of Dalaran.\nWe must be vigilant, however, knowing that source of energy lies so close at hand... Plans must be made for the future.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44,"y":40.9,"n":"Shadow Priest Allister","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"84400":{"id":84400,"t":"The knight and the lady","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"The Knight and the Lady","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nThe Knight and the Lady (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":79.4,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"8240":{"id":8240,"t":"A Bijou for Zanza","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,500, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Destroy any one of the Hakkari Bijous found in Zul'Gurub at the Altar of Zanza on Yojamba Isle. When done, speak with Vinchaxa nearby.","desc":"The destruction of the various Hakkari Bijous is of grave importance to us, so much so that we welcome outsiders of the tribe to do so for themselves!\nTake any one of the bijous that you find in Zul'Gurub to the Altar of Zanza and destroy it. For this one time alone, I will give you an additional Honor Token from our tribe; this is above and beyond what you would normally receive.\nWitness for yourself the blessings of Zanza!","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Honor Token\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Have you destroyed the bijou at the Altar of Zanza? Do so, and then you will be doubly blessed by Zanza!","done":"Excellent... each bijou we wrest away from the Blood God's minions is one step closer we all are to finally defeating them once and for all. You bring honor to the Zandalar - and yourself - through your noble actions.\nRemember ‹name›, you may always destroy the bijous you find in Zul'Gurub at the altar. For each one, you will gain recognition and an Honor Token! Just remember to have an open space in your inventory if you don't have one of the tokens already.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.5,"y":15.8,"n":"Vinchaxa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3520":{"id":3520,"t":"Screecher Spirits","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Capture the spirits of 3 screechers in Feralas, then return to Yeh'kinya in Steamwheedle Port.\nYeh'kinya's Bramble\nScreecher Spirits Collected : 0/ 3\nProvided: Yeh'kinya's Bramble","desc":"I seek the spirits of the vale screechers of Feralas. They are the cousins of an old, old god, and their spirits are linked to him.\nTake this bramble wand and go to Feralas. Find and defeat vale screechers in southern and central Feralas, then wave my bramble over their fallen bodies. This will coax their spirit to reveal itself. Touch the spirit and collect its essence.\nReturn to me with my bramble and with the collected essence, and I will tell you more of the old god of which I spoke.","rew":"Experience: 3,750","back":"Have you collected the essence of the screecher spirits, ‹name›?","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. Perhaps now it is time to reveal more...\nThere is an ancient prophecy among the trolls, where the dead god Hakkar, the Soulflayer, will one day return to this earth. Some say the coming of Hakkar will bring joy and glory to trollkind, while others believe his resurrection marks the end of all things.\nI do not believe this myth, but I do know the essence of Hakkar holds great power, and this power should be kept from those who would abuse it...\nTanaris Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":67,"y":22.4,"n":"Yeh'kinya","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"880":{"id":880,"t":"Altered Beings","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Altered Snapjaw Shells to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads.\n8 Altered Snapjaw Shell Oasis Snapjaw 80 %","desc":"Your findings are incredible, ‹name›. These oases hold properties that must come from an outside source. Or perhaps an inside one.\nI want to know how these fissures are affecting the beasts who drink from the oases' water.\nHunt oasis snapjaws at the Lushwater and Stagnant Oases. Bring me their shells so I may examine them.","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"How goes your collection? Did you get the shells?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Studying the beasts of an area can tell much about the area itself. We shall see what tale these shells tell.\nPlease accept my gratitude for your aid ... and perhaps you can use these coins. I find that I do not need them.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Tonga Runetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2880":{"id":2880,"t":"Troll Necklace Bounty","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Troll Tribal Necklaces to Fraggar Thundermantle in Aerie Peak.\n5 Troll Tribal Necklace Hitah'ya the Keeper 20 % , Morta'gya the Keeper 20 % , Mith'rethis the Enchanter 20 % , Qiaga the Keeper 20 % and 4 more","desc":"Get this straight, ‹race› - we are NOT part of the Alliance! The Wildhammers are independent, relying on deeds and actions to prove one's worth, rather than the blather of those who use jibber-jabber to bolster their do-nothing attitudes!\nIf you're looking for friends here, then prove your worth to us first! The foul trolls that choke the hillsides of the Hinterlands sometimes carry tribal necklaces. Bring five of them to me, and we'll mark it down as a step in the right direction for you.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","back":"I want five of those tribal necklaces the trolls carry on them. If you need it spelled out further, then killing one of them stands you a good chance of getting one!\nProve your worth to the Wildhammers!","done":"Now that's what I am talking about! See - these necklaces prove that you're willing to get your hands dirty. We Wildhammers value that in those we associate with.\nYou keep this up, and you'll be in our good graces yet.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":14.8,"y":44.6,"n":"Fraggar Thundermantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"7840":{"id":7840,"t":"Lard Lost His Lunch","lv":49,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Lard at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to find Lard's Lunch. Return to him when this task is complete.\nLard mentioned that he left it on the island to the north. Watch out for Vilebranch trolls.\nLard's Lunch Vilebranch Kidnapper","desc":"Lard was at secret special spot having picnic when ugly mean Vilebranch hit Lard wit da big stick. Lard run back to Revantusk but forget Lard lunch. Lard hungry. Maybe you go back to secret special spot and get Lard lunch? Lard scared. Go nort! Island der to da nort is da secret special spot.","rew":"You will receive:\nLard's Special Picnic Basket\nMoney: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"<Lard rubs his enormous belly.>\nLard so hungry.","done":"<Lard takes the huge haunch of meat from you and stuffs it in his face.>\nDis hit da spot! Tanks little one.\nLard make you special picnic basket for help Lard.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":78.1,"y":81.4,"n":"Lard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1120":{"id":1120,"t":"Get the Gnomes Drunk","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Fool's Stout to the Gnome Pit Boss.\nFool's Stout\nProvided: Fool's Stout","desc":"We need to try the Fool's Stout on one of the pit crews. If you want to try it on the gnomes, then here -- take the stout and give it to the gnome pit boss.\nAnd don't wait too long. This stout will go bad eventually.","rew":"Experience: 380","back":"Hi! You have something for me?","done":"Stout? How considerate! Thank you!\nWe shouldn't be drinking with the race coming up, but... maybe my boys could do with just a little. Besides, it can't be that strong, can it?","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.6,"y":76.9,"n":"Gnome Pit Boss","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"2240":{"id":2240,"t":"The Hidden Chamber","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read Baelog's Journal, explore the hidden chamber, then report to Prospector Stormpike.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"Now for the task at hand.\nThere is a secret chamber, the Chamber of Khaz'mul, that must be explored. The problem is that the chamber's behind a huge, locked door! It's a lucky thing I know how to open it.\nI've described everything in my journal, here on the table. My band and I are stuck here for now... so you, ‹name›, must find the chamber of Khaz'mul for us!\nRead my journal, explore the chamber, then report to Prospector Stormpike at the Explorers' League in Ironforge.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDwarven Charge Explorer's League Lodestar\nExperience: 3,900\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Do you have something to report?","done":"You have seen the Chamber of Khaz'mul? Amazing! Baelog was sure it existed, but I must admit that I had my doubts.\nThank you, ‹name›. With luck your finding will incite our leaders to renew their efforts to retake Uldaman. And if it is ever again under Ironforge control, then the secrets of the Chamber of Khaz'mul will be ours!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":23,"n":"Prospector Stormpike","e":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"1360":{"id":1360,"t":"Reclaimed Treasures","lv":43,"min":33,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get Krom Stoutarm's treasured possession from his chest in the North Common Hall of Uldaman, and bring it to him in Ironforge.\nKrom Stoutarm's Treasure Krom Stoutarm's Chest","desc":"I had myself a fine job as a digger at the Uldaman excavation site in the Badlands... that is until those blasted troggs showed up. I escaped with my hide barely intact, and nothing else. In the chaos, I left my most treasured possession. It's safe from the troggs in my chest, sure, but it's right in the thick of 'em.\nI'd be in your debt, both in honor and coin, if you could fetch it for me! A chest with my name on it is at the end of the North Common Hall. That's the one you need to get in.","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Well now, we're you able to get slap around those troggs long enough to get into my chest and nab my treasure?","done":"Ah, I feel complete again - thank you kindly.\nSome dwarves may treasure the luster of metal, and some may treasure the glint of gems... but a Stoutarm without a treasured stein in hand is hardly a Stoutarm at all!\nDun Morogh Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":22.6,"n":"Krom Stoutarm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"1680":{"id":1680,"t":"Tormus Deepforge","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tormus Deepforge.","desc":"Now that you've learned some moves, it's time to get you a decent weapon. Speak with Tormus Deepforge. He can make you a weapon I'm sure you'll like.\nYou'll find Tormus here in Ironforge, at the Great Forge.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"Muren sent you, did he? Yes, I can make you a nice weapon... but before I do that, I have a favor to ask of you.\nDon't worry. It's plenty dangerous and could mean your death; it's exactly the sort of job a warrior wants.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.4,"y":35.6,"n":"Muren Stormpike","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.9,"y":27.9,"n":"Tormus Deepforge","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1840":{"id":1840,"t":"Orm Stonehoof and the Brutal Helm","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Orm Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Orm Stonehoof is respected greatly for his skill. He will make for you the brutal helm.\nSeek him out in Thunder Bluff, near the pool by the city's great, central totem.","rew":"Experience: 1,200","done":"Greetings, warrior. I am Orm, and Thun'grim tells me you wish a helm made?\nThe Barrens Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":57.2,"y":30.3,"n":"Thun'grim Firegaze","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":39,"y":56,"n":"Orm Stonehoof","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8400":{"id":8400,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Good work, ‹name›. Thanks to you, our natural defenses in Ashenvale will remain intact for another day.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"98240":{"id":98240,"t":"Crimson crate delivery","lv":29,"min":19,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Crimson Crate to Howin Kindfeather off the road to the east of Menethil Harbor.\nProvided: Crimson Crate","desc":"Word is officially out on those whelps, ‹name›. We already have an order in!\nI'll package 'em up all nice for you, then you take it out to the customer. I know, I know; it's just one last favor, I promise!\nThese will be for one \"Howin Kindfeather\". Sent his gryphon into town of all things with a letter for the order! Says he's just off the road to the east, a bit past Whelgar's Excavation Site, if you're familiar.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Stormwind\nLevel 29 , requires level 19 Difficulty 19 25 27 32 37 Side Alliance Quest ID 98240\nThe chain\n3 quests from level 27 to 29, 5,750 XP in all.\n1 [ 27 ] Crocs of the Sky\nCollect 10 Pristine Crimson Scales and bring them to James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.\n2,200 XP\n2 [ 29 ] Crimson Crate Delivery this quest\nBring the Crimson Crate to Howin Kindfeather off the road to the east of Menethil Harbor.\n1,200 XP\n3 [ 29 ] Razormaw Needling\nCollect 10 Razormaw Incisors for Howin Kindfeather.\nHowin Kindfeather Wetlands\n2,350 XP","cats":["wetlands"]},"92640":{"id":92640,"t":"Desperate times","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar and follow her instructions.\nSpeak with Valennia Stormfist\nRecruit the Windshapers\nRecruit the High Order","desc":"Since engaging the cult in the open is not viable, our best chance is going to be to use this opportunity to attack the shrine itself. We can take Lorthuna herself off the board before she can finish her part of this scheme.\nIt so happens that Valennia has been preparing a strategy for a potential assault on the Shrine for some time now. The only problem is, we will need help.\nSpeak with Valennia for the details.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSkywatcher's Vestments Elite Peacekeeper's Leggings Broken Cultist Gloves\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","done":"Tensions between the Windshapers and High Order are high right now, but we couldn't hope to carry out this plan without both groups on board.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Talaanis Shadowsong","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92880":{"id":92880,"t":"Return to valanaar","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Yorna's Report to Valennia Stormfist in Valanaar.","desc":"I suspect it will take a bit of time for us to mop up what's left of the attackers, but our chances are far better now. Head back to Valanaar and let them know that we are stable here now.\nI can't thank you enough for your help. We'd be in much worse shape without you. I asked for reinforcements and it seems that I got a burgeoning hero instead. I'll take that.\nMay the four winds bless you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHoned Greathammer Quickblade's Dagger Balanced Quarterstaff\nExperience: 440\n+25 reputation with Windshapers\n+25 reputation with High Order","done":"<Valennia looks visibly relieved as you tell her about the status of the eastern watchtower.>\nThank the winds.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":69.6,"y":67,"n":"Yorana Windyreed","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});